# The opt-in mypyc build (PYMETTA_USE_MYPYC=1), which writes extensions beside
# the source they were built from. Shipping one would also SHADOW the pure
# Python module for every later run in the checkout, so it is ignored and
# check.sh's own build is out of tree.
metta/*.so

# coverage's data files, written by the `coverage` REPORT lane, which runs from
# this directory. One per xdist worker under `parallel = true`, plus the
# combined file.
.coverage
.coverage.*

# setuptools' own scratch, written into a member's directory whenever one is
# BUILT: the two shell proofs install a package with `uv pip install`, and the
# backend leaves `build/` and an egg-info beside the source. Shipping either
# would also shadow the module for every later run here, which is why the
# mypyc rule above exists for the same reason.
ext/*/build/
ext/*/*.egg-info/
